  "description": "1 x Thuja/Conifer  (applicants ref. T3) - Fell to ground level.\r\r1 x Apple (applicants ref. T4) - Reduce back to previous reduction points. Thin crown density by approximately 20%.\r\r1 x Horse Chestnut (applicants ref. T5) - Reduce lateral and sub-lateral branches growing towards and over Pear in the main garden by approximately 1.20-1.50m to help control encroachment.\r\r1 x Ornamental Pear (applicants ref. T6) - Reduce regrowth back into main crown structure to encourage regrowth in the central crown area.\r\r1 x Yew (applicants ref. T7) - Reduce hard back approximately 12cm to clear the gate whilst preserving secondary face to help maintain adequate fine branch scaffold for regeneration. Reduce remaining crown by up to approximately 40cm. Trim to tidy.\r\r1 x Magnolia (applicants ref. T8) - Remove including root ball.\r\r1 x Acer (applicants ref. T9) - Thin crown density by approximately 20%. Reduce (tip prune) over extended branches back into main crown structure (approximately 30cm).\r(Description amended to removed shrubs that are exempt from S211 requirement)",
